{"kind":"stack","id":"light-see","title":"Light and seeing","theme":{"background":"#fff8e1","foreground":"#263238","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c1-p","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"What do we need in order to see things?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a1","label":"Light","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}],"why":"Category: something we need to see. Light lets our eyes detect objects around us."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a2","label":"Sound","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}],"why":"Pupils often mix up hearing and seeing, since both use our senses."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a3","label":"Heat","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}],"why":"Pupils may think warm things are easier to see, mixing up heat and light."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Light"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Light is energy that lets us see. It comes from the sun, lamps and screens."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c3-p","picto":"moon"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What do we see when there is no light at all?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a1","label":"Darkness","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Category: a state of seeing. Darkness is the absence of light, so we cannot see."},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a2","label":"Blurry shapes","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Pupils may think they can still see shapes in the dark, as with a dim light."},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a3","label":"Bright colours","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Pupils may confuse dark with bright, since both are about how we see things."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"You wake at night and your room is pitch black. Do you switch on the torch or wait for your eyes to adjust?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Switch on the torch","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Wait for my eyes to adjust","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"The torch lights up your room. You can see your bed and your books clearly."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Your eyes take a while to adjust, but still almost nothing is visible. You need some light to see."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c7-p","picto":"star"},{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Which of these gives off its own light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a1","label":"The sun","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}],"why":"Category: a source of light. The sun produces its own light, unlike the moon."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a2","label":"The moon","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}],"why":"Pupils often think the moon makes its own light, when it only reflects sunlight."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a3","label":"A mirror","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}],"why":"Pupils may think shiny things glow, mixing up reflecting light with giving it off."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Dark"},{"type":"text","id":"c8-e","content":"Dark is what we see when there is no light. It is the absence of light."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c9-p","picto":"eye"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"What happens to light when it hits an object and bounces into our eyes?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a1","label":"We see the object","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}],"why":"Category: how we see things. Reflected light entering the eye lets us see the object."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a2","label":"The object disappears","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}],"why":"Pupils may think light removes objects rather than showing them."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a3","label":"The object gets heavier","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}],"why":"Pupils may confuse light with weight, thinking light adds mass."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c10-p","picto":"torch"},{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Why do we use a torch in a dark room?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a1","label":"To give light so we can see","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"Category: a reason for using light. A torch adds light so our eyes can see."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a2","label":"To make the room warmer","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"Pupils may think lights are for heating, mixing up heat and light."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a3","label":"To make the room quieter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"Pupils may connect light with sound, though light does not affect how quiet a room is."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-t","content":"Well done! You finished the light and seeing lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Remember: we need light to see, and dark is what we get when there is no light."}],"actions":[]}}
